All assets in this directory are owned by their respective copyright holders or fall under the Apache 2.0 licensing. You must have read and agreed to this license and terms in order to contribute to this project.

The reason this license exists is so that assets you do not want permitted to be copied for unrelated use of this project cannot be stolen. Though, I had to write it up in a way that confirms my legal safety and permission in using the assets given to me for this project.

---

The term "project" refers to FNF: Fireball Engine.
The term "asset" refers to media such as audio, graphics, fonts, text, or any other binary data that are seperate from actual source code.
The term "this license" refers to the written license and agreement you are currently viewing.
The term "us" refers to the main team behind the project. For example, Survikat. This does not include contributors. The main team can be defined by Survikat, and can be changed at any time.

---

Some assets fall under the Apache 2.0 license, while other assets are owned by their creators with permission to be used here in the project and cannot be reused by you - or any other entity - without granted or implied consent. Implied consent can be granted by creating forks of the project to contribute back to the original. Consent can also be given by the copyright holder.

`data` - This directory may not fall under this license, it will primarily follow the Apache 2.0 License.
`images` - This directory may not fall under the Apache 2.0 License, it will primarily follow this license.
`songs` - This directory may not fall under the Apache 2.0 License, it will primarily follow this license.
`sounds` - This directory may not fall under the Apache 2.0 License, it will primarily follow this license.
`ASSET_LICENSE.md` will list the specific licenses that specific assets take part in. If it is not listed, it will fall under its primary license for the directory it is in.
**Any other directory not specified does not fall under the Apache 2.0 License unless listed otherwise in `ASSET_LICENSE.md`**.

If you are a contributor handing off an asset to be used within the project, you confirm that the asset was created purely by you or that you have full rights to it. You agree to let us use the asset in any way, shape, or form, with or without proper attribution or authorization, but only in connection with this project, including without limitation; distribution, modifications, hosting, display, and promotional content. You understand that your only notice of contribution will be as a listed contributor on the GitHub repository, as well as potential credit within the project itself, however none are guaranteed. By submitting any changes to the original repository, you agree to these terms. This clause does not affect assets you license under the Apache 2.0 license. The licensing of the asset will depend on which directory it is located in, or by what you note down within `ASSET_LICENSE.md`.

If the asset you are contributing was made with Generative Artificial Intelligence (Generative AI), you are not allowed to contribute to the project. If you proceed to do so anyway, you must give proper notice to us of what assets specifically break this agreement if committed. If it has not yet been committed, you must take it down immediately. Failure to do so gives me the loss of my sanity which I value at $10,000,000 after taxes, which you will have to totally pay.

If you are copying the project to be used in a different personal matter - separate from contributing to the original project - you agree to remove all assets that do not fall under the Apache 2.0 license, which will likely be the majority of assets.

